# ── W11 (C6) — data-dir migration + git hygiene ────────────────────────────
# Runtime state that must NEVER be tracked (the data dir now lives OUTSIDE the
# repo via ANCHOR_DATA_DIR; these rules mirror tools/git_hygiene.classify_runtime
# so a full healthcheck cycle leaves `git status --porcelain` empty).
# the LIVE mutable R&D project registry (runtime store)
rnd_registry.json
# generated by anchor.py (not source)
dashboard.html
dashboard_api.html
# any transient scratch/session log dump
_*.log
# captured test output
pytest_stdout.txt
.write_test
# pty spike scratch outputs
test_winpty_*.txt
# host-bridge scratch outputs
bridge_test*.txt
# Volatile per-project .anchor stores (the pointer records + summaries stay
# tracked; these runtime bits never are). These mirror
# tools/git_hygiene.classify_runtime exactly: the managed-session registry, the
# per-session worktrees, discovery.json, and any nested jobs/ record.
.anchor/sessions.json
.anchor/worktrees/
.anchor/projects/*/discovery.json
.anchor/projects/*/**/jobs/
# The chamber's derived projection substrate (chamber_coldopen.cold_open_rebuild
# regenerates it from the run records; brief/projections/manifest + their locks).
.anchor/chamber/
.anchor/reaper_receipts.jsonl
.anchor/usage_ledger/
# rearch W12 (C3): the per-project append-only event journal — runtime,
# volatile, mutation-of-record (never a committed pointer record).
.anchor/projects/*/journal.jsonl
.anchor/projects/*/**/journal.jsonl_c1_before.json
# Phase-0 sidecar snapshot (spend-telemetry-2026-07) — 1GB of engine JSONL, data not code
.anchor/sidecar-archive/

# Run scratch / backups (2026-07-28) - never deliverables
test_tmp*/
*.backup.json
planning/**/pty-foreman*.log
planning/**/_*.log

# Collaborator-clone data files (v1.1.3 clone distribution): in a clone of
# the published package repo, live Anchor data accumulates UNTRACKED inside
# the package folder — ignore it so `git status` stays clean and `git pull`
# upgrades never touch user data. ROOT-ANCHORED (leading slash) so they can
# never match nested shipped content (starter/domains/, skill-internal dirs
# — the unanchored form silently dropped those from the published repo). On
# the AUTHOR repo most of these are TRACKED files, and ignore rules never
# apply to tracked files, so this section is inert for the author
# (exception: friction/ was untracked and is now hidden from status — the
# journal store is live data, not source).
/DASHBOARD.md
/INBOX.md
/PROJECTS.md
/CANCELLED.md
/SAVED_FOR_LATER.md
/WEEKLY_REVIEW.md
/domains/
/logs/
/health_reports/
/friction/

# v1.1.3 share-fix: the stale built package-v1 trees were REMOVED from git
# (61MB of duplicated product; they made agents crawl old copies and tripped
# the gemini-sdk hygiene test). The last on-disk build — the ancestor of what
# collaborators actually received — is kept LOCALLY for provenance under
# _archive/ but never re-tracked; git history (pre-v1.1.3) holds the rest.
_archive/share-package-v1-snapshot-2026-08-01/

# Anchor-side foundry-journal MACHINE records (runtime telemetry, 2026-08-04).
# foundry_journal.py writes one record per skill run under skills/<skill>/journal/
# machine/ with model_cost + inputs/outputs sidecars. Same class as rnd_jobs/ and
# .anchor/**/journal.jsonl: regenerated at runtime, grows every session, and is a
# SKILL artifact rather than Anchor source — skill work lives in the skill's own
# global location, not in this repo.
skills/
